 "All parts": "",
 "Showing {#} of {#} terms": "",
 "<0>From LLM to Agent</0>": "",
 "An LLM in a loop that chooses tools, observes the results and continues until a stop condition is met.": "",
 "Approval gate (human in the loop)": "",
 "<0>Safety & Evaluation</0>": "",
 "A gate where a person must approve an action (needs_approval = true) before the harness runs it.": "",
 "<0>Attention</0>": "",
 "Each position builds a weighted average of value vectors; the weights come from comparing its query with other positions’ keys.": "",
 "BPE (byte-pair encoding)": "",
 "<0>Tokenization</0>": "",
 "Tokenizer training: repeatedly merge the most frequent adjacent pair of symbols into one new token.": "",
 "Causal mask": "",
 "Blocks attention to future positions by setting those scores to −∞ before the softmax.": "",
 "CFG (classifier-free guidance)": "",
 "<0>ComfyUI & Diffusion</0>": "",
 "Pushes the denoising prediction away from the unconditional one, scaled by a guidance value.": "",
 "Chain of thought": "",
 "<0>Reasoning & test-time compute</0>": "",
 "The model writes intermediate reasoning tokens before its answer, spending more serial compute on the problem.": "",
 "<0>Chat APIs & Cost</0>": "",
 "Formats roles and messages into the single token sequence the model actually sees, with special tokens.": "",
 "Checkpoint": "",
 "<0>LangGraph</0>": "",
 "A saved snapshot of graph state at a step, enabling resume, interrupts and inspection.": "",
 "Chunking": "",
 "<0>RAG in Practice</0>": "",
 "Splitting documents into pieces that are embedded and retrieved separately; chunk size is a trade-off.": "",
 "<0>MLOps with ClearML</0>": "",
 "Open-source platform for experiment tracking, pipelines, data and serving.": "",
 "Node-graph tool for image-diffusion pipelines; it also exposes an HTTP API.": "",
 "<0>Inference & Serving</0>": "",
 "Maximum number of tokens (prompt plus output) the model can handle in one request.": "",
 "Cross-entropy loss": "",
 "<0>Training</0>": "",
 "Negative log-probability of the correct next token, averaged over positions. The pretraining objective.": "",
 "Generates output one token per step; each step reads the KV cache.": "",
 "DPO (direct preference optimization)": "",
 "Trains directly on preferred vs rejected replies, without a separate reward model or RL loop.": "",
 "Embedding": "",
 "<0>Embeddings & Position</0>": "",
 "Learned vector of length d_model that represents a token; a token ID selects one row of the embedding table.": "",
 "FFN (feed-forward network)": "",
 "<0>Feed-Forward & MoE</0>": "",
 "Per-token MLP after attention that transforms each position’s vector independently; much of the parameter count sits here.": "",
 "GQA (grouped-query attention)": "",
 "Groups of query heads share one key/value head, which shrinks the KV cache. MQA is the extreme case of one shared KV head.": "",
 "The ordinary code around the model: builds the context, parses tool calls, runs tools and appends the results.": "",
 "Stored keys and values of earlier tokens, so each new token does not recompute them.": "",
 "<0>LangChain</0>": "",
 "Framework of components (models, prompts, parsers, tools) for composing LLM applications.": "",
 "Framework for stateful graphs of nodes and edges; used to control agent loops, branches and handoffs.": "",
 "LCEL (LangChain Expression Language)": "",
 "Composes runnables with the pipe operator, for example prompt | model | parser.": "",
 "Uses a model with a rubric to score outputs. Practical at scale, but it needs calibration against human judgements.": "",
 "<0>Output & Sampling</0>": "",
 "Unnormalised scores, one per vocabulary entry, produced by the unembedding from the last hidden state.": "",
 "LoRA": "",
 "Freezes the base weights and trains small low-rank matrices that are added to them.": "",
 "MCP (Model Context Protocol)": "",
 "<0>Tool Calling</0>": "",
 "An open protocol for exposing tools, resources and prompts to agents through a common message format.": "",
 "MoE (mixture of experts)": "",
 "Replaces the FFN with several experts; a router sends each token to the top-k of them.": "",
 "Several heads run in parallel, each with its own d_head; their outputs are concatenated and mixed by W_o.": "",
 "Processes the whole prompt in one parallel pass and fills the KV cache.": "",
 "Prompt caching": "",
 "Reuses the processed prefix of an unchanged prompt across calls. Availability, pricing and rules vary by provider.": "",
 "Prompt injection": "",
 "Instructions hidden in untrusted content (a web page, a document or a tool result) that try to override what the user asked for.": "",
 "Quantization": "",
 "Stores weights in fewer bits (for example INT8 or {#}-bit) to save memory, usually with some accuracy cost.": "",
 "Query, Key, Value (Q, K, V)": "",
 "Three learned projections of the input: what a token looks for, what it offers for matching, and what it passes on.": "",
 "RAG (retrieval-augmented generation)": "",
 "<0>Memory & RAG</0>": "",
 "Retrieves relevant chunks and places them in the prompt before the model answers.": "",
 "Reranking": "",
 "A second-stage model rescores retrieved candidates for relevance before they reach the prompt.": "",
 "Residual stream": "",
 "<0>The Transformer Block</0>": "",
 "The per-token vector that every layer reads from and adds its output to; a shared whiteboard.": "",
 "RLHF": "",
 "Fine-tuning against a reward model trained on human preference comparisons, often with PPO.": "",
 "Scales a vector by its root-mean-square and applies a learned gain. Used before attention and the FFN in many LLMs.": "",
 "RoPE (rotary position embedding)": "",
 "Rotates Q and K by position-dependent angles so attention scores depend on relative distance.": "",
 "Scaling laws": "",
 "Empirical power-law trends linking loss to parameters, data and compute. They describe trends, not guarantees.": "",
 "SFT (supervised fine-tuning)": "",
 "Training on example (prompt, ideal reply) pairs, usually with the loss computed on the reply tokens only.": "",
 "<0>Agent Skills (SKILL.md)</0>": "",
 "A folder with a SKILL.md file of instructions, loaded progressively when a task needs it.": "",
 "Turns scores into a probability distribution: non-negative values that sum to {#}.": "",
 "Speculative decoding": "",
 "A small draft model proposes several tokens and the large model checks them in one pass.": "",
 "SwiGLU": "",
 "Gated activation used in many Llama-style models: SiLU(gate) × up, then a down projection.": "",
 "Divides the logits before the softmax. Low values make sampling near-greedy; high values flatten the distribution.": "",
 "Test-time compute": "",
 "Extra inference work (more samples, search or longer reasoning) spent to improve an answer.": "",
 "Sub-word piece of text the model reads and writes; the unit of context length and of cost.": "",
 "Token ID": "",
 "Position of a token in the vocabulary. In GPT-2, \" mat\" is {#}.": "",
 "Structured output in which the model names a tool and gives its arguments as JSON.": "",
 "Top-p (nucleus sampling)": "",
 "Keeps the smallest set of tokens whose probabilities add up to at least p, then renormalises.": "",
 "Vector database": "",
 "Stores embeddings and returns nearest neighbours, for example the top-k by cosine similarity.": "",
